   "gap": "Body 344-358 states the urn hypotheses as 'positive black weight b, red weight r and same-color reinforcement c>0'; positivity r>0 of the red weight is never stated on the route (body 344-358, annex 555-584). The conclusion that c_n are precisely the moments of beta(b/c,r/c), and its Hausdorff identification of the mixing law, require r>0 (beta(alpha,beta) is defined only for alpha,beta>0; at r=0, c_n=1 are the moments of delta_1 and no beta law exists). Feller's source urn has b black and r red balls (Feller II printed pp.229-230 = PDF pp.244-245). Owed: state the urn result with every hypothesis explicit, including r>0, or treat r=0 separately."
